<div class="callout cyan">
  <strong>One-time calibration:</strong> OSCAR computes all rotation matrices from a single forward pass
  on ~8K MMLU tokens. No per-task tuning. The resulting R_K and R_V are absorbed into the model's
  projection weights (for V) or applied as a fused prefix operation (for K) — zero overhead at inference time.
</div>
</section>

<!-- ─────────────────────────────────────── §05 ─── -->
<section id="s-system" data-code="system">
<div class="section-no">05 — System Design</div>
<h2>Mixed-precision cache layout in SGLang</h2>
<p>
  Pure INT2 for the entire KV cache breaks on "attention sink" tokens (the very first tokens) and
  the most recent tokens, which haven't yet been seen enough by calibration to have stable statistics.
  OSCAR uses a mixed-precision layout: a short BF16 window at both ends, with INT2 for the long history.
</p>

<!-- Mixed-precision layout canvas -->
<div class="vp">
  <div class="vp-head">
    <span class="vp-title">KV cache layout — token regions at decoding position t</span>
    <span class="vp-hint">drag slider to change context length</span>
  </div>
  <div class="vp-body" style="min-width:580px">
    <canvas id="layout-canvas" style="width:100%;height:160px;display:block"></canvas>
